# ── Generated run artifacts (A_71) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are pipeline OUTPUT, not source. Tracking them made the branch diff
# 1,236,261 lines across 2,483 files, which exceeds every review tool's limits
# (data/store.json alone is 385k lines). They are all reproducible by running the
# pipeline; store.json is recreated empty when absent (apps/api/src/db.ts loadState
# returns null on a missing file).
data/store.json
data/novelty-ledger.json
apps/api/data/reports/
documentation/prompts/actual/*/
results/
# stories/ is TRACKED as of 2026-08-26 — see the note at the end of this file.
logs/*.jsonl
logs/*.json


# ── stories/ is tracked, deliberately and narrowly (2026-08-26) ──────────────────────────
# The A_71 rule above untracked run artifacts because the branch diff hit 1,236,261 lines
# across 2,483 files. Manuscripts were NOT the cause of that: they are ~60KB of markdown
# each, and the whole of stories/ on this machine is 356KB across 9 files. The bulk was
# documentation/prompts/actual/*/, results/, logs/ and data/store.json, all of which stay
# ignored.
#
# Tracking manuscripts buys three things that were previously impossible from a fresh clone:
#   1. The two-laptop workflow can carry the work, not just the code.
#   2. build-opening-corpus.mjs can run anywhere. RECENT_OPENING_SITUATIONS ships EMPTY
#      today for exactly this reason, and openingCorpusReady() refuses to run A2b without
#      it — so ROADMAP-FROM-82 item 4a is blocked on a gitignore line, not on any code.
#   3. The external-read ledger stops reporting "in the manifest, no manuscript on disk"
#      for every row, which is most of what --best and --gaps currently print.
#
# NOTE: this repo is PUBLIC. Manuscripts and their chatgpt-review.txt files are visible to
# anyone. Nothing here contains credentials or personal data, but it is generated fiction
# and the reviews are cold reads of it — published, and cached by third parties even if
# later removed. If that is not wanted, make the repo private BEFORE the next push.